PARSFILE
#FullDataName Events`L. Prepare Second Set of Tests`Sine with Dwell
#CheckBox1 1    
RESET_EVENTS
#CheckBox6 0    
#CheckBox7 0    

#RingCtrl0 ~=
#RingCtrl1 >
#RingCtrl10 2
#RingCtrl11 4
*NAME1 OPT_SWD_RESTORE
*NAME2 T
*VALUE1 0
*VALUE2 0
*SPEED 80

#MiscYellow0
SWA_Sign = -1
SWA_MULT = 1
#ENDMYellow

DEFINE_EVENT OPT_SWD_RESTORE ~= 0 ; Events\Events_4041b90b-f7b0-4816-934b-2aa90d270564.par
#BlueLink0 Events`D2. Restore State for 80 km/h` Sine with Dwell` , Events`Events_4041b90b-f7b0-4816-934b-2aa90d270564

DEFINE_EVENT T > 0 ; Events\Events_de04f2bc-6ad2-41e7-a2df-bf7c640b3fdb.par
#BlueLink1 Events`B. Bring Vehicle Speed to 82 km/h` Sine with Dwell` , Events`Events_de04f2bc-6ad2-41e7-a2df-bf7c640b3fdb


#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset is loaded after the successful completion of the first set of Sine with Dwell tests. The data here prepare for the second set of tests, with steering in the opposite direction:
#
#Set the sign convention for steering to -1, and reset the multiplier SWA_MULT to 1 (for the first test in the series).
#
#If save/restore is being used, then restore the 80 km/h state D2 and continue.
#
#Otherwise, bring the speed to 82 km/h using the speed controller with dataset B.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

